<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African farmers call for wheat, barley tariffs.</title>
<headline>S.African farmers call for wheat, barley tariffs.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Winter Grain Producers Organisation (WPO) called on Tuesday for the imposition of tariffs on wheat, barley and barley malt to protect local growers from cut-price imports.</p>
<p>Chairman Chappie Ferreira said tariffs on wheat were necessary because of the relatively sharp decline in world prices recently and the large quantities of wheat that were being imported despite local surpluses.</p>
<p>The WPO also called on the Board on Tariffs and Trade to impose a tariff system for barley and malt to protect growers from subsidised imports.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
